From b13b9405b8fa4282d1bcb07822da5aaac269fc5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:22:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08074/11362] [outer-loop] add the wa30 GameAdapter -- all 25
 public games now registered

wa30 was the last public game with no adapter. It never got one as a by-product
because it was never solved by the standing loop: a 16-round OUTER-LOOP agent
probe campaign cleared it (gpt-5.6-sol v1-v8 stalled at L1; claude-fable-5 v9-v16
reached L9), which produces action sequences, not adapters. `get_adapter` then
returned None and `_live_verifier_for_adapter` raised AttributeError on it, which
read as "unsolvable" rather than "unregistered" -- so wa30 sat outside every
offline induction corpus.

L1 prefix is 33 actions, MEASURED not assumed: replayed prefixes 20..45 and took
the first that reaches L1. Sourced from the 670-action route in
results/outer_loop_fable5_wa30_probe_l9.json, gate-verified to L9 earlier today.
The adapter READS that artifact rather than pasting 33 literals, so if the banked
route is ever re-derived the adapter follows it instead of silently diverging
from the gated one.

Deliberately a replay, not a computed solver, and the docstring says so. tn36
could be state-driven because its registry entry records a full mechanic (the
bit-toggle program editor) that a solver can compute from live state. wa30's
captured RE is a per-level action sequence plus prose about NPC behaviour --
there is no per-level parameterisation to compute from, so dressing a fixed list
up as a general solver would misrepresent it.

L1 only, like most adapters here. wa30 illustrates the per-LEVEL-delta point
sharply: L2 adds a passive helper-robot NPC, L3 a fence-socket relay, L4 three
side-affiliated robots. None is expressible in an L1 action vocabulary.

Verified: builds a 12-transition induction window (33 full, 1 level-up), so wa30
can now join offline A/B corpora for the first time.

The pinning test FAILED on this change, which is the point -- it asserted wa30
was the only unregistered game and forced this edit to be conscious. Inverted to
assert all 25 are registered, with the history kept in the docstring so the
reversal is legible rather than looking like a rewrite.
